      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Igneous rocks are formed directly from the cooling and solidification of magma or lava.",
        "Sedimentary rocks are secondary rocks formed through weathering, sediment accumulation, and lithification.",
        "Metamorphic rocks result from the alteration of existing rocks under intense heat, pressure, and chemical activity.",
        "The rock cycle demonstrates how earth materials constantly transform between igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic states."
